# Documentation Skill

Reference with **@claude-skills/documentation** when writing or updating docs.

## When to use

- User asks for README, API docs, usage guide, or inline documentation
- Documenting new features, APIs, or setup steps
- Keeping docs in sync with code (e.g. after refactors)

## Principles

- Match project style (e.g. feature docs in docs/feature/<name>/)
- Include prerequisites, setup, examples, and troubleshooting where relevant
- For API docs: endpoints, params, responses, errors; OpenAPI/Swagger if used
- Do not create docs proactively unless asked; update existing docs when code changes and user expects it
